\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces X-Ray absorption spectrum of $[\text {Fe}(\text {terpy})_2]^{2+}$ (terpy: terpyridin) at the Fe K edge displaying the XANES and EXAFS regions including the background absorption contributions $\mu _0$. The inset zooms into the weak pre edge features \cite {0}.}}{3}{figure.caption.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces UV/VIS absorption spectrum of an aqueous $[\text {Fe}(\text {bipy})_3]\text {Cl}_2$ solution. The different CT transitions are indicated. The measured molar absorptivity $\epsilon $ values lie in the expected range of $10^{-4}\text {\, l}\text {\,mol}^{-1}\text {\,cm}^{-1}$ to $10^{-5}\text {\, l}\text {\,mol}^{-1}\text {\,cm}^{-1}$ for dipole-allowed transitions\cite {0}}}{4}{figure.caption.3}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The Von Hamos spectrometer in operating position. with the read-out of the Jungfrau detector as well as the settings for the position to the left.}}{5}{figure.caption.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The reference spectra plotted with provided data for different spin states.}}{6}{figure.caption.5}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The reference difference spectra with transient signals plotted with provided data for different transitions.}}{6}{figure.caption.6}%
